;; Which users' prose is sealed.
;;
;; **This migration turns it on for nobody.** The column defaults to 0 and no
;; UPDATE sets it, deliberately: every line of the seal ships inert, and the flag
;; is armed as the last act of the cutover, once the migration walker's --verify
;; has exited 0 against the sealed database. See handoffs/tracker-seal-playbook.md.
;;
;; Arming it before the data is sealed would turn every remaining plaintext body
;; into a row that cannot be saved, because the write guard refuses to let new
;; plaintext prose into a sealed user's columns.
;;
;; It is on the *user* and not on a row because that is the one question the
;; server can answer and a client cannot: a CLI guessing from a username is a
;; guess that seals somebody else's rows, and that is not recoverable.
{:id "074-add-seal-prose"
 :up ["ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN seal_prose INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0"]
 :down ["ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN seal_prose"]}
